  "text": "Esther walked in uninvited and saved a nation. Approaching the Persian king without a summons carried one penalty, and the whole empire knew it. Death. The one exception was if he held out the golden sceptre. And Esther tells Mordecai, I have not been called to come in unto the king these thirty days. She is the queen and she has not been summoned in a month. Mordecai's answer is brutal and kind at once. Do not think you will escape in the king's house any more than the rest of the Jews. And then, if you hold your peace, deliverance will arise from another place, but you and your father's house will be destroyed. He never says God will fail. He says rescue is coming and she might miss it. Then, who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for such a time as this? A question, not a command. So she fasts three days with all the Jews in Shushan, and says, if I perish, I perish. On the third day she puts on her royal apparel and stands in the inner court. And the king holds out the sceptre. She lives. And then she throws the dinner party that flipped an empire.",
